## Deliverable acceptance

The Software stack and dependency decision register is accepted.

Evidence:

- merged G0 governance and stack pull request;
- `studentship_software_stack_decision_register_v0.1.md`;
- completed `SWE-ENV-STACK-WP1`;
- downstream handoff to:
  - `SWE-ENV-DEP-WP1`;
  - `SWE-ENV-BLD-WP1`;
  - `SWE-ENV-LIC-WP1`.

`SWE-ENV-STACK` is complete.

Acceptance evidence for `SWE-R2D-STA` is complete in merged PR #250 / squash commit `5ad288ed48900c376ec9310c1a0ab07461cb35f9`.

Issue-tree preflight found no authorised child Work Packages beneath `SWE-R2D-STA`; only parent deliverable #47 matched the WBS search.

State implementation:

- `RegionalConservedState` owns mesh-bound cell fields for `h`, `hu` and `hv`;
- units are `m`, `m2/s`, `m2/s`;
- `ShallowWaterStatePolicy` validates gravity, dry depth, depth tolerance and normal tolerance;
- local state validation rejects nonfinite values and depths below `-epsilon_h`;
- dry states canonicalise to `(0,0,0)`;
- primitive recovery returns `u=q_x/h`, `v=q_y/h` only for wet states and never divides by dry/zero depth;
- state construction and validation are transactional.

Verification:

- policy validation, wet/dry primitive recovery, negative-depth rejection and dry canonicalisation passed;
- mesh-wide state construction, filled construction, units, clone behavior and failed canonicalisation transactionality passed;
- GCC and Clang workflows passed with 55/55 tests;
- previous 46 CTest tests remain passing;
- existing architecture validators passed.

Acceptance evidence for `SWE-R2D-FLX` is complete in merged PR #250 / squash commit `5ad288ed48900c376ec9310c1a0ab07461cb35f9`.

Issue-tree preflight found no authorised child Work Packages beneath `SWE-R2D-FLX`; only parent deliverable #48 matched the WBS search.

Flux implementation:

- owner-oriented face normals are derived from accepted FVM face-area vectors;
- physical shallow-water normal flux implements the homogeneous NLSWE flux;
- characteristic speed is shared by Rusanov dissipation, residual spectral sums and CFL estimation;
- baseline Rusanov flux implements `0.5(F_L+F_R)-0.5 alpha (U_R-U_L)`;
- dry/dry, wet/dry, dry/wet and wet/wet states produce finite deterministic results;
- HLL and HLLC remain deferred, with no placeholder implementations added.

Verification:

- still-water, x-flow, y-flow and oblique-normal analytical flux tests passed;
- signal-speed analytical and normal-reversal tests passed;
- Rusanov consistency and reversal-conservation errors are `0.0` within `1e-12`;
- dry/dry returns zero flux and zero signal speed;
- GCC and Clang workflows passed with 55/55 tests;
- existing architecture validators passed.

Progress from merged PR #251 / squash commit `d723eda`:

Completed:
- static cell-centred bathymetry;
- free-surface derivation;
- hydrostatic bathymetric source treatment;
- lake-at-rest well balancing.

Still outstanding:
- Manning friction;
- Coriolis;
- any other accepted optional source terms.

Progress from merged PR #250 / squash commit `5ad288ed48900c376ec9310c1a0ab07461cb35f9`:

- added reusable CFL spectral-sum timestep estimation;
- added absent-timestep semantics for all-zero spectral sums rather than returning infinity;
- added deterministic limiting-cell selection;
- added a reusable transactional forward-Euler stage primitive;
- verified zero-residual preservation, analytical update behavior, candidate-state rejection, dry canonicalisation and pointer stability.

`SWE-R2D-TIM` remains open for the accepted full CFL control/time-integration deliverable.

Progress from merged PR #250 / squash commit `5ad288ed48900c376ec9310c1a0ab07461cb35f9`:

- added `RegionalResidual` with integrated outward mass and momentum residual components;
- added reusable residual workspace storage for boundary exterior states, residuals and spectral sums;
- implemented one-face Rusanov traversal with opposite owner/neighbour internal contributions;
- assembled scalar boundary exterior states from depth, x-momentum and y-momentum boundary sets;
- verified constant wet/dry residual preservation, named-boundary failure transactionality, internal-face cancellation, spectral sums and maximum signal speed.

`SWE-R2D-SOL` remains open for the integrated solve loop, diagnostics and output-production deliverable.

